+.. setting:: broker_pool_acquire_timeout
+
+``broker_pool_acquire_timeout``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. versionadded:: 5.6
+
+Default: :const:`None`.
+
+The maximum number of seconds to wait for a connection (or producer) to
+become available from the broker connection pool when sending a task.
+
+When the pool is exhausted, task dispatch blocks until a connection is
+released. If this setting is set to a number of seconds, the wait is limited
+to that many seconds; if no connection becomes available in time, an
+:exc:`~celery.exceptions.OperationalError` is raised. The default of
+:const:`None` blocks indefinitely.
+
+This setting complements :setting:`broker_pool_limit`: if you see errors
+about all connections being in use, consider increasing
+:setting:`broker_pool_limit` or this timeout.
+
 .. setting:: broker_connection_timeout
 
 ``broker_connection_timeout``
